  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In first step bromination reaction will take place, since amine group is strong activating group, bromination will take place at all ortho and para positions. Then it will give diazonium salt which on reaction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will give sym-tribromobenzene.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8658d9f9-c0bb-4e65-89fa-011c5d531c77-ce3544cb-bf80-49e6-8f07-50ef9fb642d6-9709570_Solution.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 322px;\" /></p>",
